    "body": "- [ ] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n# What does this PR do?\n\nA required CODEOWNERS team remains in `pending_expert_teams` or `pending_final_teams` when its member lookup fails or returns no members. Expanding that team to reviewers produces an empty set, however, and only the reviewer set reaches the label state machine. An unreviewed PR can consequently receive or retain `Approved` after a GitHub membership error.\n\nPreserve unsatisfied teams explicitly in the pending sets passed to the state machine. This keeps Expert Review and Final Review pending and revokes stale Approved labels until the required approval is known.\n\nThe tests drive the production tracker with real PyGithub imported and mocked API boundaries; no GitHub mutations occur. They cover failed/empty lookups in all three stages for expert/final teams, plus known-team approval and pending-review controls.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Reproduced on unchanged production code: focused regressions **12 failed and 3 passed controls**.\n- After the fix, the same focused tests **15 passed** in the Linux Python 3.12 CPU tooling container.\n- `uv run --no-project --python /opt/cpu-review/bin/python isort` on both changed files; Black 26 check, isort check, Ruff, and Python compile checks passed.\n- Required `BASE_REF=main CHECK_ONLY=true SKIP_DOCS=false bash tools/autoformat.sh` completed successfully with the pinned Black 26.3.0, isort 5.13.2, Pylint 3.2.6, and Ruff 0.9.10. Its nonblocking mypy step reports 1 pre-existing source errors, confirmed on unchanged baseline; no new mypy diagnostics.\n- GPU training validation is not covered by these CPU orchestration tests.\n\n```bash\npython -m pytest -q tests/test_utils/python_scripts/test_swap_pr_labels_required_teams.py\n```\n\n## Issue tracking\n\nLinked issue: none; this is a small, reproduced bug fix, not a new feature or GPU kernel.\n\n## Contribution process\n\n- [x] Added relevant focused regressions.\n- [ ] Added GPU functional tests.\n- [x] Ran the repository formatter.\n\nAI-assisted draft; human author review and NVIDIA GPU/full CI validation are pending. The personal author-review checkbox is left unchecked.\n",
